CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract foo --replace-call-with-contract h _ --unwind 2 --unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[.*unwind.*\] .*: FAILURE$
--
The check that the assigns clause of h's contract, which replaces the call,
is included in foo's loops over h's 6 targets: DFCC unwinds it as far as the
largest assigns clause, which counts the replacing contracts' too (foo's has
1 target), rather than as --unwind says.
